{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545423-the-end-of-the-warriors-of-glycon","id":1545423,"title":"The end of the Warriors of Glycon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-05T18:28:06-08:00","id":1545423,"title":"The end of the Warriors of Glycon","content":"Hello there!<br /> <br /> VDA20 introduced two new Setite bloodlines, the Witches of Echidna and the then-ruling-the-clan Warriors of Glycon. The former go extinct within the VDA20 bloodline and the events occurring around 1244 CE; the latter are said to be bound for extinction as well, but at a later point in time. While the Witches resurface somehow in V5 or V20 (can't remember which), the Warriors of Glycon are never heard of in material for the modern nights or the Victorian Age to my knowledge.<br /> <br /> Of course, we have &quot;Warrior Setites&quot;, but those exist already in VDA20 and are merely vampires from the Priest bloodline extensively trained in Potence, to the point of replacing their Obfuscate (Warriors of Glycon are militarily stronger since they have Obfuscate, Potence and Serpentis, making them a true menace - especially with VDA20 Serpentis -, while Warrior Setites keep the social engagement through Presence).<br /> <br /> V20 also gives us the a Path of Enlightenment for Warrior Setites which is pretty cool and is claimed to date back to Egypt's subjugation to the the Macedonian and Roman Empires. This may be a lie, or it may be a Path that is not mentioned in VDA20 material but which could make sense for either or both the Warriors of Glycon and Warrior Setites - but the xenophobic side of the Path is more suited to the Warrior Setites, who seem more trapped in Egyptian nationalism than the older Warriors of Glycon, who seem more at home with an heclectic and syncretic Setism centered on both Mother Echidna and Father Typhon, like the Witches, to some extent. <br /> <br /> The extinction of the Warriors of Glycon was prophetised by the Witches, like their own demise, just for a later date, and ascribed to the trickery of the Priests.<br /> <br /> These are the facts known to me. Any theory as to how and when the Warriors of Glycon might have gone extinct? I understand there is no current publications for Victorian Age or any other historical period between the Dark Ages and the time of the Masquerade, otherwise one could have developed the story of their end as part of the Victorian Age timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}